$STOP = 'the and for with that this from have has are was were will would can could should must may our you your their they them its not but into than then also more any all each other such only own same very just about over under between through while during before after above below who what when where which how why one two three four five six seven eight nine ten etc per via within across able ability including include includes plus both either well new like get gets make makes work works working team teams role roles join looking seeking strong good great ideal candidate candidates company position job years year experience required requirements preferred responsibilities les des une dans pour avec sont sur par aux est nous vous der die das und mit von nicht ein eine für sind sie wir auf bei oder zum zur del los las una por con que para como pero más gli per che non sono nel della delle uma dos com não mais ser você nós';
$stop = array_flip(explode(' ', $STOP));
function words(string $t): array { preg_match_all('/[\p{L}\p{N}][\p{L}\p{N}+#.\/-]*[\p{L}\p{N}+#]|[\p{L}\p{N}]/u', mb_strtolower($t), $m); return $m[0]; }

// ---- cv -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
if ($sub === 'cv') {
    $MON = ['jan'=>1,'gen'=>1,'feb'=>2,'fev'=>2,'fév'=>2,'mar'=>3,'mär'=>3,'apr'=>4,'avr'=>4,'abr'=>4,'may'=>5,'mai'=>5,'mag'=>5,'jun'=>6,'giu'=>6,'jul'=>7,'lug'=>7,'aug'=>8,'aou'=>8,'aoû'=>8,'ago'=>8,'sep'=>9,'set'=>9,'oct'=>10,'out'=>10,'ott'=>10,'okt'=>10,'nov'=>11,'dec'=>12,'dez'=>12,'dic'=>12,'déc'=>12];
    $mre = '[A-Za-zäéûÄ]{3,9}\.?\s+\d{4}'; $D = "(?:$mre|\\d{1,2}[\\/.]\\d{4}|\\d{4}-\\d{1,2}|\\d{4})"; $NOW = 'present|now|current|today|ongoing|heute|aktuell|pr[ée]sent|actuel|aujourd.hui|oggi|presente|atual|actualidad|hoy|hasta hoy';
